---
// Terms, privacy and cookies on 1 page. The structure follows the vetted Laissez-Faire Group legal pages,
// rewritten for what this site really does. Each part is a list of [title, text] rows.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site';
const mail = `<a href="mailto:${SITE.email}">${SITE.email}</a>`;
const CO = SITE.company;
const parts = [
  { id: 'privacy', title: 'Privacy', rows: [
    ['Forms', `When you use the contact or booking form, I get your name, your email, your company or event if you add it, what you wrote, the type of request and, on the booking form, what you need and the event date. The site also saves the time, your browser type and your country. I use it to reply. It is stored with Cloudflare under your email, so a second message from you links to the first. I get a Telegram alert with the type of request, your name and line 1 of your message. I never store your raw IP address, only a salted hash of it, so I can stop spam floods.`],
    ['What you send', `You are responsible for what you send through a form. Don't send other people's personal information unless they said you could.`],
    ['Spam check', `Forms use Cloudflare Turnstile to tell people from bots. Turnstile looks at signals from your browser to decide, without tracking you across sites.`],
    ['Analytics', `The site uses Google Analytics 4 to count visits and see which pages get read: things like pages viewed, time on page, the site that sent you, your device type and your rough location from your IP address. If you are in the EU, the EEA, the UK or Switzerland, or the site can't tell where you are, no analytics cookies are set until you say yes in the banner. Elsewhere, analytics is on by default. You can change your answer at any time with Cookie settings at the bottom of every page.`],
    ['Videos', `Videos play in YouTube's own player, and YouTube sets its own cookies when that player loads. In the EU, EEA, UK and Switzerland the player loads only after you click the video. Elsewhere it loads with the page.`],
    ['How I use it', `To reply to you, to send you what you asked for, to see which pages and videos are useful, to keep the site working and to protect it from abuse. I don't sell your information, and I don't use it for advertising.`],
    ['Who sees it', `The services that run the site: Cloudflare (hosting, forms and the spam check), Google (Analytics and YouTube) and Telegram (my private alert). If you write about work with Laissez-Faire Group, I may pass your message to the LFG team. I may also share information if the law requires it, to prevent fraud or abuse, or to protect someone's rights or safety. If the business is ever merged or sold, your information moves with it under these same rules.`],
    ['Links', `This site links to other sites, like YouTube, X and LinkedIn. They have their own privacy policies, and I'm not responsible for what they do.`],
    ['Where it lives', `Form messages are stored with Cloudflare in the United States. Google and Telegram may handle their part in other countries. If you use the site from another country, your information is sent to the United States. I keep messages only as long as I need them to reply and follow up. Ask me and I'll delete yours sooner.`],
    ['Security', `I follow industry practice: encrypted connections, no raw IP addresses stored, and access limited to me. No system is 100% secure, so I can't promise absolute security.`],
    ['Do Not Track', `The site doesn't respond to browser Do Not Track signals. Cookie settings at the bottom of every page and your browser's own settings are how you control analytics.`],
    ['Children', `This site is for a general audience. I don't knowingly collect information from anyone under 16. If you think a child sent me information, email me and I'll delete it.`],
    ['Your rights', `You can ask what I hold about you, ask me to correct it or ask me to delete it. If you are in the EU, the EEA, the UK or Switzerland, you have these rights under the GDPR and UK GDPR, along with the right to object, to limit how I use your information, to get a copy you can take elsewhere, to withdraw consent, and to complain to your data protection authority. There, I only use your information when you agreed to it, when I need it to do what you asked, when I have a fair business reason that doesn't override your rights, or when the law requires it. I'll answer within 1 month. Email ${mail} with your name and what you need.`],
    ['Changes', `If this policy changes, the date at the top changes too. Using the site after an update means you accept the new version.`],
  ] },
  { id: 'cookies', title: 'Cookies', rows: [
    ['What cookies are', `Small text files a site saves on your device. They help a site work, remember your choices and show how people use it.`],
    ['What this site uses', `Needed to run the site: your answer to the consent banner and your country code, saved in your browser's storage, and whatever Cloudflare needs for security and the spam check. These can't be switched off. Analytics: Google Analytics 4, only with your consent where the law asks for it. Video: YouTube's player sets its own cookies when it loads. Advertising or cross-site tracking: none.`],
    ['Managing cookies', `Use Cookie settings at the bottom of every page to change your analytics answer. You can also block or delete cookies in your browser settings. The site still works without them.`],
    ['Changes', `This list gets updated when the site changes. The current version is always on this page.`],
  ] },
  { id: 'terms', title: 'Terms', rows: [
    ['Using this site', `By using action.ceo you agree to these terms and to the privacy and cookie sections above. If you don't agree, please don't use the site. I may change the terms at any time, and using the site after a change means you accept it.`],
    ['Who can use it', `Anyone can read and watch. To book me or do business through this site you need to be 18 or older, able to agree to these terms for yourself or your organization, and not barred from doing so by any law or sanction. I can refuse or end access for anyone.`],
    ['What you can do', `Read and watch what's here, share links to it, and get in touch about working together.`],
    ["What you can't do", `Break the law with it, try to get into parts of the site or its systems you have no right to, spread malware, scrape or crawl it with bots without permission, overload it, collect other people's personal information from it, or pass yourself off as me or as working with me.`],
    ['Who owns the content', `The text, videos, images, logos and design belong to ${CO} or to those who own or licensed them, like guests, event partners and Laissez-Faire Group. You may view them for personal, non-commercial use. Don't copy, resell or rework them, and don't use the Action name or logo, without written permission.`],
    ['Not financial advice', `Everything here is general information and my opinion. It is not investment, legal, tax or accounting advice, and it is not an offer to buy or sell anything. Crypto and other digital assets are speculative and volatile, and past results don't predict future ones. Nothing on this site is a recommendation to buy, hold or sell any token. I am not a registered investment adviser, broker, dealer, exchange or custodian. Check the rules where you live and get independent professional advice before you act.`],
    ['Web3 and AI tech', `The technology I cover is new and can fail. I don't promise that any project, network, smart contract or tool I talk about is secure, lawful or fit for your use.`],
    ['Other sites', `Links to other sites are there for convenience. I don't endorse them and I'm not responsible for them. Use them at your own risk and read their terms.`],
    ['Working with me', `Using this site or sending a form doesn't make you a client. A working relationship starts only when a written agreement is signed, and until then talks and proposals aren't binding. If that agreement and these terms disagree, the agreement wins for that work.`],
    ['No guarantees', `The site is provided "as is" and "as available", with no warranties of any kind, including accuracy, availability or fitness for a purpose. You use it at your own risk.`],
    ['Limit of liability', `As far as the law allows, ${CO} and the people who work with it are not liable for indirect, special, punitive or consequential damages, or for lost profits, data or opportunities, even if warned they could happen. Total liability is capped at the greater of US$100 or what you paid ${CO} in the 12 months before the claim.`],
    ['If you cause a claim', `If your use of the site, your breach of these terms or the law, or something you sent leads to a claim against ${CO}, you agree to cover the losses and costs, including reasonable legal fees.`],
    ['Law and disputes', `These terms follow the law of the place where ${CO} is registered. If there's a dispute, we first try to settle it in good faith after written notice. If that fails within 30 days, it goes to binding arbitration in English, run by an institution we both agree on or, failing that, the ICC. As far as the law allows, claims are brought one by one, not as a class action. ${CO} can still go to court for an order that protects its content, name or confidential information.`],
    ['Ending access', `I can suspend or end access to the site at any time, for any reason, without notice. The parts of these terms that should outlast that, like ownership, the disclaimers and the liability limits, still apply.`],
    ['The fine print', `These terms, with the privacy and cookie sections and any signed agreement, are the whole agreement about your use of the site. If a part can't be enforced, it is narrowed as little as needed and the rest stands. Not enforcing a term once doesn't waive it. You can't transfer your rights under these terms without written consent; ${CO} can. Nobody is liable for delays caused by things outside their control. The terms are in English, and the English version wins over any translation.`],
    ['Contact', `Questions about any of this: ${mail}.`],
  ] },
];
---
<Base page="privacy">
<Header current="" />
<header class="legal-top">
<h1 class="legal-h1">Terms and privacy.</h1>
<p class="legal-lead">The short version: I collect what you send me through a form, plus analytics about your visit. I never sell it. Nothing on this site is financial advice.</p>
<p class="legal-meta">This site, action.ceo, is run by {CO}. On this page, "I" and "me" mean {CO} and Action, the person behind it. Last updated Nov 19, 2026.</p>
<nav aria-label="On this page" class="legal-nav">{parts.map((p) => <a href={`#${p.id}`} class="btn-line">{p.title}</a>)}</nav>
</header>
{parts.map((p) => (
<section class="rv legal-part" id={p.id} aria-labelledby={`${p.id}-h`}>
<h2 class="sec-h" id={`${p.id}-h`}>{p.title}</h2>
{p.rows.map(([k, v]) => (<div class="legal-row"><h3 class="legal-k">{k}</h3><div class="legal-v" set:html={v}></div></div>))}
</section>
))}
</Base>
